Package: PhysioNetPhysiology
Type: Package
Title: Network Physiology and Time-Delay-Stability Organ-Interaction Networks
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Yusuke",
           family = "Matsui",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for Network Physiology: the study of dynamic interactions
    among diverse physiological systems (brain, heart, respiration, muscle).
    Implements Time Delay Stability (TDS) analysis to identify stable dynamic
    couplings between signals, builds organ-interaction networks whose links are
    significance-tested against phase-randomised surrogates, and quantifies how
    those networks reconfigure across physiological states (e.g. sleep stages).
    Designed to operate on the multimodal PhysioExperiment data model, but the
    core engine works on plain multivariate time series. Methods follow
    Bashan et al. (2012) <doi:10.1038/ncomms1705> and
    Bartsch et al. (2015) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0142143>.
